    {
      "id": "5pismy7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Composition of the Atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nitrogen (78%) and Oxygen (21%) constitute nearly 99% of the clean, dry air in the atmosphere.",
        "The Troposphere contains almost all water vapor and aerosols, making it the seat of all weather phenomena.",
        "The Stratosphere extends up to 50 km and hosts the Ozone layer, which shields Earth from harmful ultraviolet solar radiation.",
        "The Mesosphere is the coldest atmospheric layer, reaching temperatures as low as -90°C where most meteors burn up.",
        "The Thermosphere houses the Ionosphere, facilitating long-distance radio communication by reflecting radio waves back to Earth."
      ],
      "id": "dldhfek"
    },
