      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0vhgmmn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Troposphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r79ekiu",
      "content": "• Lowest layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "The atmosphere is an envelope of gases surrounding the earth, held in place by Earth's gravitational force.",
      "id": "lltfmm2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "487k24v",
      "content": "• Contains about 75% of atmospheric mass."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s8t1ihs",
      "content": "• All weather phenomena such as clouds, rain and storms occur here."
    },
    {
      "id": "coudhp3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Stratosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tfzigqq",
      "content": "• Located above the troposphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8vccj7i",
      "content": "• Contains the ozone layer that absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3j92suj",
      "content": "• Jet aircraft often fly in this layer."
    },
    {
      "id": "bph6z6w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Mesosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Atmospheric Layer",
        "Height Range",
        "Key Characteristic"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Troposphere",
          "0 - 13 km",
          "Contains weather phenomena and experiences normal lapse rate"
        ],
        [
          "Stratosphere",
          "13 - 50 km",
          "Contains Ozone layer; ideal for flying jet aeroplanes"
        ],
        [
          "Mesosphere",
          "50 - 80 km",
          "Coldest layer; burns up incoming meteorites"
        ],
        [
          "Thermosphere",
          "80 - 400 km",
          "Contains Ionosphere; reflects radio waves back to Earth"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "rr9zx43"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lhok2st",
      "content": "• Third layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ayzph3v",
      "content": "• Meteors burn up due to friction in this layer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f9sh6v6",
      "content": "• It is the coldest layer."
    },
    {
      "id": "2znztmf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Thermosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vy66ykd",
      "content": "• Temperature rises sharply with height."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q6v3rya",
      "content": "• Contains ionized gases forming the ionosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7ruvfr1",
      "content": "• Important for radio communication."
    },
    {
      "id": "n9kzjsy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Exosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0buqftw",
      "content": "• Outermost layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oug828s",
      "content": "• Gradually merges into outer space."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Temperature decreases in the Troposphere at a rate of 6.5°C per 1,000 meters elevation, known as the Normal Lapse Rate.",
        "Aeroplanes fly in the lower Stratosphere to avoid weather disruptions occurring in the Troposphere.",
        "The Ionosphere (located in the Thermosphere) contains electrically charged particles called ions that reflect radio waves back to Earth."
      ],
      "id": "vroy46q"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3ys0n0x",
      "content": "• Contains very thin air."
    },
    {
      "id": "b8g96c3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ajpqgjd",
      "content": "• Nitrogen is the most abundant gas in the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uodegsd",
      "content": "• Ozone layer is located in the stratosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7wknp9h",
      "content": "• Troposphere contains most weather phenomena."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "voubsyg",
      "content": "• Mesosphere is the coldest layer."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}